# interplay_lifetime_held_heap_deleted_heap_buffer: An exec that copies a heap buffer out waits on the gate while the worker FIFO (child 2) deletes (37) the heap, or the heap buffer. The heap buffer was filled with 0xa1s before. Released, the exec lists the heap and the buffer, so what was deleted is made again from its record: a new heap is paged from the guest pages, but the live heap buffer keeps the old heap and its fill; a new heap buffer is placed in the live heap at the same offset and reads the fill too. In-process the fill never reaches the guest pages; in the service it is in them at once.
